.TH TERRAIN-STUDIO 1 "21 November 2026" "Terrain Studio 0.3.0"
.SH NAME
terrain-studio \- compose and render 3D landscapes and abstract scenes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B terrain-studio
.RI [ project.terrain | scene.BRC ]
.br
.B terrain-studio render
.I output.png
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B terrain-studio list-maps
.I BRYCE2.iso
.br
.B terrain-studio list-brc-terrains
.I SCENE.BRC
.br
.B terrain-studio convert-brc
.I SCENE.BRC OUTPUT.terrain
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the graphical scene editor, render a PNG without a desktop session,
list the TIFF heightmaps available in a Bryce 2 ISO 9660 disc image,
list elevation grids in a Bryce 2 composite scene, or convert supported
geometry and camera settings to an editable Terrain Studio project.
.SH RENDER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --preset " name"
Start from mirage, checker, mercury, alpine, canyon or coast.
.TP
.BI --scene " project.terrain"
Render a saved Terrain Studio scene.
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Set the unsigned 32-bit seed used for scene generation and procedural materials.
.TP
.BI --size " WIDTHxHEIGHT"
Set the output size (between 16 and 4096 per side). Defaults to the size
stored in the project when available, or 960x720.
.TP
.BI --heightmap " image"
Import a grayscale or color image as terrain.
.TP
.BI --iso " BRYCE2.iso"
Read a heightmap from the disc image. Use with
.BR --map .
.TP
.BI --map " NAME.TIF"
Select the TIFF heightmap within the disc's TERRAIN folder.
.TP
.BI --brc " SCENE.BRC"
Import an elevation grid from a Bryce 2 scene. Other scene settings
come from the selected Terrain Studio project or preset.
.TP
.BI --brc-scene " SCENE.BRC"
Restore the placed terrain, spheres, cubes and perspective camera.
.TP
.BI --terrain-index " ID"
Select a Bryce 2 terrain resource by its table index. Defaults to the
first terrain at the largest available resolution.
.TP
.B --draft
Use a single sample per pixel for a faster preview render.
.SH FILES
.I *.terrain
are Terrain Studio scene projects. They store the terrain and all object,
atmosphere and camera settings needed to rerender the scene.
